{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And when virgins were gathered a second time.</b> The meaning is that this was the second time; already Mordecai was sitting at the king's gate, for this was in the seventh year of the reign, and the feast on account of Vashti was in the third year. And the Sages said that Israel incurred the death penalty because they ate at the king's table and drank of his wine."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:47.847690974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}